We are building the next generation of our Demand-Side Platform (DSP), enabling advertisers to access premium digital inventory through high-performance programmatic technology.
Our bidder is at the heart of the platform, making real-time auction decisions and powering global advertising campaigns. We are looking for a Lead Backend Engineer (Go) to shape its architecture, performance, and future direction, while driving technical quality and helping grow the engineering team.
Requirements

• Extensive experience in backend software development with Go;

• Strong understanding of distributed systems and microservice architectures;

• Experience building and operating high-performance, low-latency backend services;

• Proven ability to identify, analyze, and resolve complex performance and scalability challenges;

• Ability to work independently and drive initiatives from concept to production;

• Strong communication skills and experience working closely with Product;

• Leadership experience or strong potential and readiness to step into a technical leadership role.

Will be a plus

• Experience with AdTech or Programmatic Advertising (auction mechanics, high-scale decisioning);

• Experience with Google Cloud Platform (GCP), Kubernetes, and cloud-native environments;

• Familiarity with data-intensive applications, analytics platforms, and large-scale aggregations;

• Understanding of Machine Learning concepts and production ML integrations;

• Experience leading technical initiatives, mentoring engineers, or working with distributed external teams.

Responsibilities

• Design, develop, and maintain high-performance backend services in Go;

• Analyze and optimize distributed systems and microservice-based architectures;

• Drive engineering quality through code reviews, technical leadership, and best practices;

• Contribute to architecture decisions, technology selection, and platform strategy;

• Collaborate closely with Product Managers to translate business needs into scalable technical solutions;

• Work alongside Data Engineering and Machine Learning teams to integrate data-driven capabilities into bidder workflows;

• Help establish a strong engineering culture built around ownership, accountability, and continuous improvement.

What we offer

• 22 paid vacation days per year;

• 10 paid sick leave days per year;

• Paid public holidays;

• English coverage: client-sponsored group classes and GD English Speaking Club;

• Help and support from our caring HR team;

• Continuous professional growth and collaboration with talented colleagues;

• Competitive compensation for your efforts.

